{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yubikit\/loggingguide"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"YubiKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Logging"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/LoggingGuide"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No setup is required. YubiKit defaults to "},{"code":"debug","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on stdout when compiled with "},{"code":"DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"code":"info","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on stderr otherwise. You can override either default:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import YubiKit","import Logging","","\/\/ Show warnings and errors.","YubiKit.Logs.configure(logLevel: .warning)","","\/\/ Use your preferred backend.","YubiKit.Logs.configure(logLevel: .debug) { label in","    StreamLogHandler.standardOutput(label: label)","}","","\/\/ Turn logging off.","YubiKit.Logs.configure { _ in SwiftLogNoOpLogHandler() }","","\/\/ Restore defaults.","YubiKit.Logs.configure()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/apple\/swift-log"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"Logging","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to use its backend types. Any SwiftLog "},{"code":"LogHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can be supplied by the factory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call replaces both settings. Omitting the factory restores YubiKit’s backend;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"omitting the level uses the selected handler’s level. Changes apply to existing sessions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though logs already in progress may use the previous settings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"YubiKit’s configuration does not affect other libraries. To share your app’s backend,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass its factory explicitly; global "},{"code":"LoggingSystem.bootstrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not select YubiKit’s backend."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Factories may run concurrently and must not log through YubiKit themselves."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Traffic logging","anchor":"Traffic-logging"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["YubiKit.Logs.configure(logLevel: .trace)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Raw traffic and SCP plaintext logs require "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"YubiKit to be compiled with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEBUG"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Neither configuration nor a custom backend can enable them in other builds."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Custom connections are responsible for their own traffic logging."}]},{"style":"warning","name":"Warning","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Debug logs can include account names and credential identifiers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Trace logs can include PINs, credentials, and cryptographic keys. Protect or redact logs before sharing them."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Custom backends","anchor":"Custom-backends"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Labels identify categories, such as "},{"code":"com.yubico.YubiKit.OATH","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"com.yubico.YubiKit.FIDO","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Metadata carries details such as byte counts and error codes; the default backend displays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"these as "},{"code":"key=value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pairs. Message wording and metadata keys are not a stable API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your backend controls formatting, storage, and export. YubiKit does not retain log messages."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose YubiKit’s log level and backend with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/Logs\/configure(logLevel:factory:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Preparing your project","identifiers":["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/Logs"],"anchor":"Preparing-your-project","generated":true}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit"]]},"references":{"doc://yubikit-swift.YubiKit/documentation/YubiKit/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Prepare your project to connect to the YubiKey via NFC, SmartCard, Lightning and USB HID."}],"title":"Getting Started","url":"\/documentation\/yubikit\/gettingstarted","role":"article"},"doc://yubikit-swift.YubiKit/documentation/YubiKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Connect and run commands on the different applications on a YubiKey. The framework support connecting using NFC, Lightning and USB.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","images":[{"iden